---
title: PawPal+ final system architecture
---
classDiagram
    %% Final design, Phase 6. Matches pawpal_system.py member for member.
    %%
    %% Changed from the Phase 1 draft:
    %%   - Priority became an IntEnum so it sorts directly; Frequency added
    %%   - ScheduledTask / SkippedTask / DailyPlan added, so a plan carries
    %%     clock times, what was dropped, and the reason for each
    %%   - Conflict added, so overlaps are reported instead of only avoided
    %%   - Task gained due_date + recurrence, so completing one queues the next
    %%   - Scheduler lost its own copy of the time budget and reads the Owner
    %%
    %% Dependencies point one way only: app.py (UI) and main.py (CLI) both
    %% import this layer, and nothing here imports Streamlit. That is what lets
    %% the same logic be driven from a browser, a terminal and the tests.

    class Owner {
        +str name
        +int minutes_available
        +list~str~ preferences
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet) None
        +remove_pet(pet_name) bool
        +remove_pet_at(index) bool
        +get_pet(pet_name) Pet
        +all_tasks() list~Task~
        +tasks_by_pet() dict
        +filter_tasks(pet_name, completed, priority, frequency, due_on) list~Task~
        +prefers(task) bool
        +save_to_json(path) None
        +load_from_json(path) Owner
    }

    class Pet {
        +str name
        +str species
        +str breed
        +int age_years
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) None
        +remove_task(task_title) bool
        +remove_task_at(index) bool
        +get_task(task_title) Task
        +pending_tasks() list~Task~
        +completed_tasks() list~Task~
        +tasks_due_on(day) list~Task~
        +filter_tasks(completed, priority, frequency, due_on) list~Task~
        +complete_task(task, today) Task
        +uncomplete_task(task, today) bool
        +minutes_needed_on(day) int
    }

    class Task {
        +str title
        +int duration_minutes
        +Priority priority
        +Frequency frequency
        +int weekly_day
        +time preferred_time
        +date due_date
        +bool completed
        +str task_id
        +str follow_up_id
        +timedelta duration
        +bool is_anchored
        +mark_complete() None
        +mark_incomplete() None
        +is_due_on(day) bool
        +window_on(day) tuple
        +next_due_date(after) date
        +next_occurrence(after) Task
    }

    class Priority {
        <<enumeration>>
        LOW
        MEDIUM
        HIGH
        +parse(value) Priority
    }

    class Frequency {
        <<enumeration>>
        DAILY
        WEEKLY
        +parse(value) Frequency
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +time day_start
        +time day_end
        +build_plan(owner, pet, day) DailyPlan
        +build_plans(owner, day) list~DailyPlan~
        +next_available_slot(owner, duration_minutes, day) time
        +sort_by_time(tasks) list~Task~
        +sort_by_priority(tasks) list~Task~
        +find_conflicts(owner, day) list~Conflict~
        +conflict_warnings(owner, day) list~str~
        +explain(plan) str
    }

    class DailyPlan {
        +str pet_name
        +date day
        +list~ScheduledTask~ scheduled
        +list~SkippedTask~ skipped
        +int budget_minutes
        +int minutes_used
        +int minutes_remaining
        +bool is_empty
    }

    class ScheduledTask {
        +Task task
        +time start_time
        +str reason
        +end_time() time
    }

    class SkippedTask {
        +Task task
        +str reason
    }

    class Conflict {
        +str first_pet
        +Task first
        +str second_pet
        +Task second
        +date day
        +str message
    }

    Owner "1" --> "*" Pet : owns
    Pet "1" --> "*" Task : needs care
    Task --> Priority : ranked by
    Task --> Frequency : recurs by
    Task ..> Task : next_occurrence() queues

    Scheduler ..> Owner : reads budget and preferences
    Scheduler ..> Pet : reads tasks due today
    Scheduler ..> DailyPlan : produces one per pet
    Scheduler ..> Conflict : reports overlaps

    DailyPlan "1" --> "*" ScheduledTask : contains
    DailyPlan "1" --> "*" SkippedTask : records
    ScheduledTask --> Task : places at a time
    SkippedTask --> Task : explains dropping
    Conflict --> Task : names the clashing pair

    note for Scheduler "Stateless apart from the day window.<br/>All pets share one timeline and one<br/>time budget, so nothing double-books<br/>the owner and priority is compared<br/>across the whole household."
    note for Task "Every task recurs. Completing one<br/>queues its next occurrence rather<br/>than disappearing."
